# Family Tree & Social Rules
## Nuclear Family (Close Family)Appear in family tree:- Grandparents (paternal/maternal)- Father, Mother- Siblings (brothers/sisters)- Spouse- Children- Grandchildren
## General Family (Extended)Do NOT appear in family tree. Appear only in "All Family Members" list:- Uncles, Aunts- Cousins- Nephews, Nieces
## Family Tree Graph Model- Table `family_members` – stores each member (id, name, gender, age, is_dead, is_placeholder).- Table `family_relationships` – stores edges (source_id, target_id, relation_type: parent, child, spouse, sibling).- Tree rendered using D3.js.- User’s own node is centred.- Empty placeholders have "Add +" button.
## Family Activation Form (New Users)First time user clicks Family Tree tab, show form:- Relationship status: Unmarried, Married, Single‑Parent, Widowed- Children? (Yes/No – only if Married, Single‑Parent, Widowed)- Father’s Name, Mother’s Name- Siblings? (Yes/No – then number of brothers and sisters, with name fields)- Removed: Grandparents section (can be added later via tree).
## Connection Requests- Users can send Family or Social connection requests using **Account ID (public_id)**.- Requests appear in recipient's notification bell + inbox.- Recipient can Accept or Reject.- After acceptance, member appears in appropriate list (Family tree or Social list).
## Dead Members- Family members can be marked "deceased" (Admin only? Actually user can mark).- Deceased members appear in tree with grey text and a icon (no strikethrough).- Marking deceased is done via a single button ("Mark Deceased") that lists all living members (checkbox modal).
## Removal Rules- **Admin**: Can remove any family member at any time.- **Non‑admin**: Can remove family member directly within 2 days of adding.- **After 2 days**: User must send removal request to Admin (with reason).- Admin approves/rejects via "Family member removal request queue".
## Social Tab- List of accepted social connections (friends, colleagues).- Add social connection via Account ID (no relationship dropdown).- Remove button available for any connection.
